Applied by tools/build-toolchain.sh when the binutils pin is on branch
amiga-2.46.  The pin is still amiga-2.39.0 (tools/build-toolchain.sh:39), which
selects tools/patches/binutils/ instead; this set is what a pin that moves gets.

Against bebbo's binutils-gdb, branch amiga-2.46, commit
a50544a917284847c99e97d41c69ece9d5cb2fef (https://franke.ms/git/bebbo/binutils-gdb).

WHAT IT FIXES

`m68k-amigaos-strip` on a hunk executable writes it back with no HUNK_RELOC32
at all -- exit 0, no diagnostic -- and LoadSeg() then relocates nothing, so
every absolute address keeps its link-time value.  `objcopy --strip-all` does
the same and `-K` does not save it.  Measured on the pinned GCC 16.2.0b: a
four-line C file loses 278 of 278 relocations, and one cross arm of this tree
shipped 40 of 77 images unrelocated.  tools/check-hunk-relocs.sh is what
catches it; nothing else does.

Two causes, both in copy_relocations_in_section():

  1. bebbo's amiga-2.39.0 carries `#ifdef TARGET_AMIGA || 1` in the
     strip_symbols == STRIP_ALL reloc filter (2.39 objcopy.c:4367), which keeps
     every relocation.  The amiga-2.46 rebase dropped it.
  2. Upstream 2.46 added an earlier short-circuit that forces relsize = 0 for
     the same case before the filter is reached.

Both are correct for ELF, where relocations a stripped image still needs live
in sections objcopy copies as contents.  On hunk they are the HUNK_RELOC32 that
this function is the only writer of.

MEASURED, 2026-08-27, a 2.46 toolchain built with this applied over the pinned
GCC 16.2.0b:

  strip 2.46, WITHOUT this patch
    check=ok           file=r2.exe hunks=3 relocs=324 bytes=18612
    check=UNRELOCATED  file=r2.exe hunks=3 relocs=0   bytes=13524   rc=1

  strip 2.46, WITH this patch
    check=ok           file=r.exe  hunks=3 relocs=324 bytes=18612
    check=ok           file=r.exe  hunks=3 relocs=324 bytes=14876   rc=0

  the whole tree, -DAMINETXDUO_LTO=OFF, built by that toolchain
    hunk_relocs=clean images=118 build=build/bu246                  rc=0

The LTO arms still do not link: neither diff in tools/patches/binutils/ applies
to 2.46, and that work would have to be redone against 2.46's own LTO support
before the pin could move.

diff --git a/binutils/objcopy.c b/binutils/objcopy.c
index fdd8bd11..1d3487a2 100644
--- a/binutils/objcopy.c
+++ b/binutils/objcopy.c
@@ -4527,8 +4527,13 @@ copy_relocations_in_section (bfd *ibfd, sec_ptr isection, bfd *obfd)
   /* Core files and DWO files do not need to be relocated.  */
   if (bfd_get_format (obfd) == bfd_core
       || strip_symbols == STRIP_NONDWO
+#ifndef TARGET_AMIGA
+      /* A hunk executable carries its relocations as HUNK_RELOC32, not as a
+	 section the copy loop reproduces, so dropping them here leaves an
+	 image LoadSeg() will not relocate.  */
       || (strip_symbols == STRIP_ALL
 	  && htab_elements (keep_specific_htab) == 0)
+#endif
       || discard_relocations (ibfd, isection))
     relsize = 0;
   else
@@ -4586,8 +4591,12 @@ copy_relocations_in_section (bfd *ibfd, sec_ptr isection, bfd *obfd)
 	    if (relpp[i]->sym_ptr_ptr
 		/* PR 20096 */
 		&& *relpp[i]->sym_ptr_ptr
-		&& is_specified_symbol (bfd_asymbol_name (*relpp[i]->sym_ptr_ptr),
-					keep_specific_htab))
+		&& (is_specified_symbol (bfd_asymbol_name (*relpp[i]->sym_ptr_ptr),
+					 keep_specific_htab)
+#ifdef TARGET_AMIGA
+		    || 1
+#endif
+		   ))
 	      *w_relpp++ = relpp[i];
 	  relcount = w_relpp - relpp;
 	  *w_relpp = 0;
